adbd for q2-coda --dev builds (docs/adb.md), applied by tools/thirdparty.py's build_adbd to
android-tools 4.2.2+git20130218 with Debian's patches (3ubuntu41) applied. Licensed as the code it
changes, Apache-2.0. It carries Buildroot's fixes for building adbd off Ubuntu (package/android-tools
0002, 0003, 0004, 0006, 0007, 0014 and 0015 at 8a25ff3f: no glib or D-Bus, adb's own base64, cdefs,
capset and prctl) and then the Q2's changes:

- adb_auth_client.c: RSA key authentication always on. Authorized keys are /mnt/data/adb_keys and, while
  the card is mounted, /mnt/mmc/adb_keys, read for every connection. An unknown key goes to the UI over
  the socket /tmp/q2adb-ui as Android's framework gets it ("PK<key>", answered "OK" or anything else);
  with no UI connected (the Wi-Fi adbd connects none) it is refused. RSA_verify is libmincrypt's (fetched beside the source), not
  OpenSSL's, whose RSA_verify the Debian build linked by mistake. transport.c tells it when a computer
  it asked about goes.
- adb.c: USB FunctionFS, or with --tcp PORT that TCP port alone (adb over Wi-Fi, a second process; it
  never asks the UI, and each computer let in and each service it opens renames a new
  /tmp/q2remote.used into place for Smart Wi-Fi's hold); no smartsocket on 5037, no JDWP socket, no
  privilege drop (a root shell, behind authorization), umask 022, the keys reloaded at each CNXN.
- transport_local.c: the Wi-Fi adbd keeps at most 8 connections, each with TCP keep-alive, and its
  remote_close leaves the transport's socketpair end to the registration's remove, which closes it (a
  second close there shut a newer connection's socket, or the listening one).
- usb_linux_client.c: FunctionFS v2 descriptors with Microsoft OS descriptors (compatible ID WINUSB,
  DeviceInterfaceGUID adb's), so Windows binds WinUSB itself; ep0 kept open for adbd's lifetime, as
  closing it makes the kernel unbind the gadget; host control requests answered.
- services.c, sockets.c: shell:, exec: (no pty, for adb exec-out), sync:, reboot: (busybox's) and
  the tcp:/local: forwards; Android's framebuffer:, jdwp:, log:, remount:, backup:, restore:,
  recover:, root:, usb:, tcpip: and dev: services removed.
- file_sync_service.c: utimes for utime.

